    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The full suite passes (`BUILD SUCCESS`), including the new `coreDerivesAgeBand` test.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `ageBand` derivation for `POST /api/owners` / `GET /api/owners/{id}`. The request may now include an optional ISO `birthDate`, and the owner response reports `ageBand` computed against `registrationDate`.\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added `birthDate` (optional input, `format: date`) to the `OwnerFields` schema and a read-only `ageBand` string to the `Owner` schema. These regenerate `OwnerFieldsDto`/`OwnerDto` at build time.\n\n2. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added the `birthDate` field (`@Column(name = \"birth_date\")`) with getter/setter so it persists between create and read. MapStruct's `toOwner(OwnerFieldsDto)` maps it by name automatically.\n\n3. **`model/AgeBand.java`** (new) \u2014 a small derivation helper mirroring the existing `MembershipLevel`/`ContactPreference`/`Locality` pattern: `MINOR` (<18), `ADULT` (18\u201364), `SENIOR` (65+), measured with `Period.between(birthDate, registrationDate)`; returns `null` when no `birthDate` was supplied (falls back to today if registrationDate is absent).\n\n4. **`mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added `@Mapping(target = \"ageBand\", expression = \"\u2026AgeBand.of(owner)\")`, consistent with the other derived-field expressions.\n\n5. **DB schemas** (`hsqldb`, `h2`, `mysql`, `postgres`) \u2014 added a `birth_date DATE` column to the `owners` table (tests run on the hsqldb profile).\n\nNo `@RestController`/`@Transactional` were introduced \u2014 the change stays within the DTO/model/mapper layers that the existing OfficeFloor create/read pipelines already use.\n\nNote: I added the `birth_date` column to all four DB schema files for consistency, but only the hsqldb schema is exercised by the test profile \u2014 I haven't run against mysql/postgres.",
